null score) is EXCLUDED, not zeroed -- zeroing it gives 0.352846 and would have reproduced
the artifact for the wrong reason.

At source: exp5764 (exp5726.run_reason_cell_budget, reused verbatim) prompts on the WHOLE
window and grades on the WHOLE window -- in-sample fit. exp5766 round 0 reaches induce via
execute_bounded_llm_reinduction, whose run_cegis_cell never passes proposal_transitions, so
it falls back to _proposal_prefix (first 2/3), and is graded by select_trusted_world_model
on _split_prefix_heldout's last 1/3 -- disjoint. Verified the two cuts land on the same
index for n in {3,4,5,9,12,25}. Scored like-for-like against prefix_accuracy -- recorded
beside heldout_accuracy on every round record, never read -- 0.378487 vs 0.319444, p = 1.0.

ONE CORRECTION TO THE CONFIRMATION. It proposed keying the guard on the ROW SET. Done
literally that refuses the CORRECT like-for-like comparison it itself identified, because
whole_window and prompt_overlapping_prefix are different row sets. The guard keys on the
RELATION to the prompt (in_sample / out_of_sample), so the valid comparison is permitted and
only the in-sample-vs-out-of-sample subtraction is refused. Mutation 3 proves this is
load-bearing rather than decorative.

